+## Conventions
+
+### Command prefix aliasing
+
+Slash commands in this repo use the canonical `geno-` prefix (e.g., `/geno-mine`, `/geno-mine-extract`). The prefix users type at runtime (`/gt-`, `/geno-`, or bare `/`) is configured in `~/.geno/config.yaml` under `aliases.command_prefix` and applied at install time by `geno-tools install`. Never hardcode a `/gt-` prefix in `SKILL.md` descriptions, `GENO.md`, or any committed file.
+
+### Adding a new skill
+
+1. Create a directory under `skills/` named `geno-mine-{sub-skillset}-{skill}` (e.g., `geno-mine-export-validate`).
+2. Write a `SKILL.md` inside it with YAML frontmatter: `name`, `description`, `allowed-tools`.
+3. Update `skills/geno-mine/SKILL.md` umbrella description to list the new skill.
+4. Add the skill to the Skills table in this file.
+5. Bump the version in `genotools.yaml`, `pyproject.toml`, `package.json`, and `geno_mine/__init__.py`.
+
+### Versioning
+
+`genotools.yaml` is the canonical version source. Keep `pyproject.toml` `project.version`, `package.json` `version`, and `geno_mine/__init__.py` `__version__` in sync with it. Bump the version whenever skills are added, removed, or behavior changes.
+
 ## Privacy
 
 All processing is local (zero telemetry). The filter stage:
